# members.txt — team roster (git host usernames, one per line)
#
# Copy this file to `members.txt` and add your team's usernames:
#     cp members.txt.example members.txt
#
# Each username must have an SSH public key registered on your git host
# (fetched from {GIT_HOST_URL}/{username}.keys). Every listed member can
# decrypt the team store.
#
#   Add a member:    append their username, then: git add -f members.txt && commit && push
#   Remove a member: delete their username, commit, push (members re-encrypt on next push)
#
# Example:
# alice
# bob
